{"availability":"available","full":"elahlabs/elah","name":"elah","description":"Elah is a browser-native video editing framework and toolkit for building high-performance editing experiences on the web. It provides modular editor infrastructure, timeline systems, playback architecture, and developer-focused APIs designed for modern video applications.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":62,"forks":8,"created":"2026-06-09T08:06:03Z","updated":"2026-10-08T14:09:07Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.elah.dev/","topics":[],"demo":"https://www.elah.dev/playgrounds","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.676Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.676Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.676Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.676Z","stars":62,"forks":8}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-native, frame-accurate video editing engine for the web. A framework-agnostic core — timeline, WebGL2 renderer, media pipeline, and MP4 export — with thin UI bindings on top. React is the first UI layer (shipping today); the engine knows nothing about it, so React Native and other frameworks can bind to the same core. The same engine also runs headless: @elah/cli builds and renders projects from the command line, a Node API, or a long-lived HTTP render server (elah serve) — so AI backends can generate videos with no UI at all. Works for any aspect ratio (9:16 Reels, 16:9 YouTube,…","[]( [](./BUNDLESTRATEGY.md) [](./LICENSE) [](","Website · Docs · Playground · Changelog · npm · Discord"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elahlabs/elah/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1a3515267550b06b39b920f0bb9a8151daf6cf61884e9b79852c2825b909fbef","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.837Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.837Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A browser-native, frame-accurate video editing engine for the web. A fr